# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Compute a Néel quench {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"
msgstr "3. Kira kuens Néel {#3-compute-a-néel-quench}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can now watch the bosons move under a quench. The dynamics start from a **Néel pattern**: the sites of a checkerboard are alternately\n"
"filled with one boson (black circles in the drawing below) and empty (white circles), so half of the sites are occupied. At\n"
"time zero, the state is a single bit string, which is easy to prepare (one `X` gate per occupied site). It is not an eigenstate of\n"
"the hopping Hamiltonian: every bond of the lattice joins an occupied and an empty site, so every bond can move a boson,\n"
"and the state starts to change right away. Preparing a simple state and then letting it evolve under a Hamiltonian that it\n"
"is not an eigenstate of is called a **quench**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini anda boleh menyaksikan boson bergerak di bawah kuens. Dinamik bermula daripada **corak Néel**: tapak papan dam diisi secara berselang-seli\n"
"dengan satu boson (bulatan hitam dalam lukisan di bawah) dan kosong (bulatan putih), jadi separuh daripada tapak diduduki. Pada\n"
"masa sifar, keadaan ialah satu rentetan bit, yang mudah disediakan (satu get `X` bagi setiap tapak yang diduduki). Ia bukan keadaan eigen\n"
"Hamiltonian lompatan: setiap ikatan kekisi menyambungkan tapak yang diduduki dan tapak yang kosong, jadi setiap ikatan boleh menggerakkan boson,\n"
"dan keadaan mula berubah serta-merta. Menyediakan keadaan mudah dan kemudian membiarkannya berevolusi di bawah Hamiltonian yang\n"
"bukan keadaan eigennya dipanggil **kuens**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d8ccb302-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the lattice is bipartite, a hop always moves a boson to the other sublattice of the checkerboard. This suggests the\n"
"observable to follow, the **staggered density imbalance**\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh kerana kekisi ialah dwipartit, lompatan sentiasa menggerakkan boson ke subkekisi papan dam yang satu lagi. Ini mencadangkan\n"
"cerapan yang perlu diikuti, iaitu **ketidakseimbangan ketumpatan berselang-seli**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\mathcal I(t) = \\frac1N \\sum_i (-1)^{x_i+y_i}\\,\\bigl(2\\langle n_i\\rangle(t) - 1\\bigr) = \\frac{2}{N}\\bigl(N_A(t) - N_B(t)\\bigr),$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $N_A$ and $N_B$ are the numbers of bosons on the two sublattices. It measures how many bosons are still on the\n"
"sublattice they started on. It starts at $\\mathcal I = 1$ and, as the bosons spread over the lattice, falls and then\n"
"fluctuates around zero, where neither sublattice is preferred. On hardware, it is cheap to measure, because it only needs\n"
"the occupation of each site, that is, single-qubit $Z$ measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan $N_A$ dan $N_B$ ialah bilangan boson pada kedua-dua subkekisi. Ia mengukur berapa banyak boson masih berada pada\n"
"subkekisi tempat ia bermula. Ia bermula pada $\\mathcal I = 1$ dan, apabila boson tersebar merentasi kekisi, jatuh dan kemudian\n"
"berubah-ubah sekitar sifar, yang mana tiada subkekisi diutamakan. Pada perkakasan, ia murah untuk diukur, kerana ia hanya memerlukan\n"
"pendudukan setiap tapak, iaitu pengukuran $Z$ qubit tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The later plots of the observable behavior also show the density of individual sites.\n"
"In one dimension, this quench is a free-fermion problem, but on a square lattice it is not (as discussed in section 1), so the exact evolution of the $4\\times4$ lattice below is the reference. The hard-core Hilbert space is the set of bit strings, and $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ moves a bit. Build $H$ as a sparse matrix with plain numpy and evolve with `expm_multiply`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Plot kelakuan cerapan yang kemudian juga menunjukkan ketumpatan tapak individu.\n"
"Dalam satu dimensi, kuens ini ialah masalah fermion bebas, tetapi pada kekisi segi empat sama ia bukan (seperti yang dibincangkan dalam bahagian 1), jadi evolusi tepat kekisi $4\\times4$ di bawah ialah rujukan. Ruang Hilbert teras keras ialah set rentetan bit, dan $b_i^\\dagger b_j$ menggerakkan satu bit. Bina $H$ sebagai matriks jarang dengan numpy biasa dan berevolusi dengan `expm_multiply`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, compute the exact reference.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kira rujukan tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, check the `InitializeModes` gate, which also confirms that the mode-to-qubit encoding is correct.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, semak get `InitializeModes`, yang juga mengesahkan bahawa pengekodan mod-ke-qubit adalah betul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now compute the Trotterized curves. A circuit is one first-order Trotter step of length $dt$ (all four colors once), applied\n"
"$T/dt$ times; `trotter_series` returns the site densities at every multiple of $dt$. The cell after it turns the densities of\n"
"the exact and of the Trotterized evolution into the three observables to plot.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kira lengkung Trotter. Satu litar ialah satu langkah Trotter tertib pertama sepanjang $dt$ (keempat-empat warna sekali), dikenakan\n"
"$T/dt$ kali; `trotter_series` memulangkan ketumpatan tapak pada setiap gandaan $dt$. Sel selepasnya menukar ketumpatan\n"
"evolusi tepat dan evolusi Trotter kepada tiga cerapan untuk diplot.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/dd335add-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/dd335add-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $dt = T/\\text{steps}$ is the length of one Trotter step, so the legend gives both. All three panels show all three step\n"
"sizes. The smaller the step, the closer the circuit follows the exact curve. The coarsest step, $dt = 0.5$, visibly misses it in places, and even $dt = 0.1$ shows a small wobble on the corner site near $t \\approx 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $dt = T/\\text{steps}$ ialah panjang satu langkah Trotter, jadi legenda memberikan kedua-duanya. Ketiga-tiga panel menunjukkan ketiga-tiga saiz\n"
"langkah. Semakin kecil langkah, semakin hampir litar mengikuti lengkung tepat. Langkah terkasar, $dt = 0.5$, jelas tersasar di beberapa tempat, dan walaupun $dt = 0.1$ menunjukkan sedikit goyangan pada tapak sudut sekitar $t \\approx 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Quantify the Trotter error {#4-quantify-the-trotter-error}"
msgstr "4. Kuantifikasi ralat Trotter {#4-quantify-the-trotter-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The only numerical error of the circuit is the **Trotter error between the colors** at the bosonic level. The other two\n"
"places where an error could creep in are exact by construction:\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu-satunya ralat berangka litar ialah **ralat Trotter antara warna** pada peringkat bosonik. Dua tempat lain\n"
"yang mungkin menyebabkan ralat adalah tepat melalui pembinaan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The qubit side.** The Pauli terms of one color commute, because the bonds of a color share no site. Synthesizing a color\n"
"therefore needs no further approximation, and the circuit is the ordered product of the exact color exponentials.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sebelah qubit.** Sebutan Pauli bagi satu warna saling kekomutatif, kerana ikatan sesuatu warna tidak berkongsi tapak. Mensintesis satu warna\n"
"oleh itu tidak memerlukan penghampiran lanjut, dan litar ialah hasil darab tertib eksponen warna yang tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The encoding.** At $d = 2$, the four `LevelEncoding`s are different representations of the same two-level system, so they\n"
"give the same circuit up to cost (section 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengekodan.** Pada $d = 2$, keempat-empat `LevelEncoding` ialah perwakilan berbeza bagi sistem dua aras yang sama, jadi\n"
"menghasilkan litar yang sama sehingga kos (bahagian 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is no \"truncation\" error either: the cutoff $d = 2$ *defines* this model (section 1). It is not a numerical\n"
"approximation of something larger.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tiada ralat \"pemangkasan\" juga: penggalan $d = 2$ *mentakrifkan* model ini (bahagian 1). Ia bukan\n"
"penghampiran berangka bagi sesuatu yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section explores `BosonicSuzukiTrotter`. It measures the Trotter error against the exact reference of section 3 at one final time, $T = 2$, versus\n"
"the number of steps, for first and for second order. It uses $T = 2$, not the end of the curves above, on purpose: by\n"
"$t = 3$, the signal has decayed close to its long-time value, so the error there is small and scatters from one step count to\n"
"the next. At $T = 2$, the dynamics are still pronounced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini meneroka `BosonicSuzukiTrotter`. Ia mengukur ralat Trotter berbanding rujukan tepat dari bahagian 3 pada satu masa akhir, $T = 2$, melawan\n"
"bilangan langkah, untuk peringkat pertama dan kedua. Ia menggunakan $T = 2$, bukan hujung lengkung di atas, dengan sengaja: pada\n"
"$t = 3$, isyarat telah mereput hampir kepada nilai jangka panjangnya, jadi ralat di situ kecil dan bertaburan dari satu bilangan langkah\n"
"ke yang seterusnya. Pada $T = 2$, dinamiknya masih jelas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Is the bosonic level needed for this error?** For hard-core bosons, the qubit operator is only $-\\tfrac12(XX + YY)$ per bond,\n"
"so you can also hand it to Qiskit as **one** `PauliEvolutionGate`, without any groups, and let Qiskit's `SuzukiTrotter` product formula split it. A product formula applies the terms in the order it is\n"
"given, so the order decides which terms are exponentiated together. Try three: the terms sorted by edge color (the grouping\n"
"that the bosonic circuit knows), the terms bond by bond, and `preserve_order=False`, which lets Qiskit reorder the terms\n"
"itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Adakah aras bosonik diperlukan untuk ralat ini?** Bagi boson teras keras, operator qubit hanyalah $-\\tfrac12(XX + YY)$ bagi setiap ikatan,\n"
"jadi anda juga boleh memberikannya kepada Qiskit sebagai **satu** `PauliEvolutionGate`, tanpa sebarang kumpulan, dan membiarkan formula hasil darab `SuzukiTrotter` Qiskit memecahkannya. Formula hasil darab menggunakan sebutan mengikut susunan yang\n"
"diberikan, jadi susunan menentukan sebutan mana yang dieksponenkan bersama. Cuba tiga: sebutan yang disusun mengikut warna tepi (pengelompokan\n"
"yang diketahui oleh litar bosonik), sebutan ikatan demi ikatan, dan `preserve_order=False`, yang membenarkan Qiskit menyusun semula sebutan\n"
"sendiri.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/11884bb1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/11884bb1-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Left:** the dotted gray lines are the ideal slopes $-1$ and $-2$, and the fitted slope over the last three points of each\n"
"curve is in the legend. The slopes approach the ideal values only once the step is small enough; with few steps, the error is\n"
"outside the asymptotic regime.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kiri:** garis kelabu bertitik ialah cerun unggul $-1$ dan $-2$, dan cerun terpadan pada tiga titik terakhir setiap\n"
"lengkung ada dalam legenda. Cerun menghampiri nilai unggul hanya apabila langkah cukup kecil; dengan langkah yang sedikit, ralat\n"
"berada di luar rejim asimptot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Right:** the same errors against the two-qubit depth of the whole circuit, for the same step\n"
"counts. A second-order step has more blocks (14 against 8 layers for one step), but adjacent identical blocks of neighboring\n"
"repetitions merge. For large errors (one or two steps), first order is the cheaper way to reach a given error. Below an error of about $10^{-1}$, second order is cheaper.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kanan:** ralat yang sama melawan kedalaman dua-qubit bagi keseluruhan litar, untuk bilangan\n"
"langkah yang sama. Satu langkah peringkat kedua mempunyai lebih banyak blok (14 berbanding 8 lapisan untuk satu langkah), tetapi blok serupa bersebelahan bagi\n"
"pengulangan jiran bergabung. Untuk ralat besar (satu atau dua langkah), peringkat pertama ialah cara yang lebih murah untuk mencapai ralat tertentu. Di bawah ralat kira-kira $10^{-1}$, peringkat kedua lebih murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Single gates.** The dashed curves are the single `PauliEvolutionGate` with `SuzukiTrotter` of order 1 (green) and 2 (blue). Each\n"
"ordering of the Pauli terms has its own marker and a lighter tint of the color. With the terms sorted by color (crosses), the\n"
"single gate lies exactly on the bosonic curve of the same order: it is the same product formula. In the other two orderings,\n"
"it is a different formula with a different error, which can be several times larger or (at one or two steps) smaller. But the\n"
"**order of magnitude and the scaling match** the bosonic circuit: the first-order curves fall with the ideal slope $-1$ and the\n"
"second-order curves with $-2$, and at 32 steps all three orderings are within a factor of about three of each other. So the Trotter\n"
"error does not decide between the approaches. What differs is the cost (right panel, and the next section): at equal error,\n"
"the squares (medium tint) need a much larger depth, and the triangles (lightest tint) roughly twice the depth of the crosses. At the bosonic level, the\n"
"grouping is part of the operator, so there is no ordering to choose by hand, which makes for a much more ergonomic workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gate tunggal.** Lengkung putus-putus ialah `PauliEvolutionGate` tunggal dengan `SuzukiTrotter` peringkat 1 (hijau) dan 2 (biru). Setiap\n"
"susunan sebutan Pauli mempunyai penanda sendiri dan warna yang lebih cerah. Dengan sebutan disusun mengikut warna (pangkah),\n"
"gate tunggal terletak tepat pada lengkung bosonik peringkat yang sama: ia ialah formula hasil darab yang sama. Dalam dua susunan lain,\n"
"ia ialah formula berbeza dengan ralat berbeza, yang boleh beberapa kali ganda lebih besar atau (pada satu atau dua langkah) lebih kecil. Tetapi\n"
"**magnitud dan penskalaan sepadan** dengan litar bosonik: lengkung peringkat pertama menurun dengan cerun unggul $-1$ dan lengkung\n"
"peringkat kedua dengan $-2$, dan pada 32 langkah ketiga-tiga susunan berada dalam lingkungan faktor kira-kira tiga antara satu sama lain. Jadi ralat\n"
"Trotter tidak menentukan pilihan antara pendekatan. Yang berbeza ialah kos (panel kanan, dan bahagian seterusnya): pada ralat yang sama,\n"
"segi empat sama (warna sederhana) memerlukan kedalaman yang jauh lebih besar, dan segi tiga (warna paling cerah) kira-kira dua kali ganda kedalaman pangkah. Pada aras bosonik,\n"
"pengelompokan ialah sebahagian daripada operator, jadi tiada susunan untuk dipilih secara manual, yang menjadikan aliran kerja jauh lebih ergonomik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Scale with system size {#5-scale-with-system-size}"
msgstr "5. Skala dengan saiz sistem {#5-scale-with-system-size}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section investigates how cost scales with the lattice size. Since one Trotter step is one $XX+YY$ layer per color, whatever the\n"
"number of sites, the two-qubit **depth should be flat** in the lattice size while the **gate count grows** with the number of\n"
"bonds. The sizes go up to $10\\times12$, the whole Nighthawk chip in the compact codes. The unary codes need two qubits\n"
"per mode, so they stop at the sizes that fit in 120 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ini menyiasat bagaimana kos berskala dengan saiz kekisi. Oleh kerana satu langkah Trotter ialah satu lapisan $XX+YY$ bagi setiap warna, tidak kira\n"
"bilangan tapak, **kedalaman** dua-qubit **sepatutnya rata** terhadap saiz kekisi manakala **bilangan gate meningkat** dengan bilangan\n"
"ikatan. Saiznya sehingga $10\\times12$, iaitu keseluruhan cip Nighthawk dalam kod padat. Kod unari memerlukan dua qubit\n"
"bagi setiap mod, jadi ia berhenti pada saiz yang muat dalam 120 qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d4dbf1ea-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/d4dbf1ea-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The compact code has a flat depth from $3\\times3$ on (every color is a layer of side-by-side $XX+YY$ rotations; the $2\\times2$\n"
"lattice has only two colors, so its depth is half) and a gate count that grows with the number of bonds.\n"
"The unary codes are an order of magnitude more expensive in both. The reason is simple: in the compact codes, a bond maps to one $XX$ and\n"
"one $YY$ term on the two qubits of the bond with equal coefficients, that is, an $XX+YY$ rotation (two `cz`). In the unary codes, each\n"
"mode has two qubits (one per level), and the hop expands into several weight-4 Pauli strings on the four qubits of both\n"
"modes. They all commute, so nothing is saved by commutation. The ratio is a property of the encoding at $d = 2$, and it does\n"
"not change with the lattice size. At $d = 2$, the standard-binary and Gray codes are the same code, and the projected and\n"
"unprojected unary codes emit the same operator, so the compact curve stands for both pairs.\n"
"**Why Trotterize at the bosonic level?** The dashed curves are the same Trotter steps as one `PauliEvolutionGate` over the qubit\n"
"operator (section 4), in green for first order and blue for second order. The solid blue curve is the second-order bosonic circuit,\n"
"the solid green curve the first-order one from above. The single gate with the terms sorted by color (crosses) lies exactly on the\n"
"bosonic curve of its order: a flat depth (8 for first order, 14 for second order) and the minimal gate count (as in the previous section). Qiskit does not find\n"
"that grouping by itself. If the terms are listed bond by bond (squares), the gate count is the same, but the layers are not packed\n"
"and the depth grows with the lattice (at $10\\times12$ it is 84 against 8 for first order and 166 against 14 for second order).\n"
"With `preserve_order=False` (triangles), Qiskit does find commuting terms and the depth stays flat, but it treats the XX and the YY\n"
"term of a bond as separate rotations, so it needs about a third more two-qubit gates and twice the depth. So the bosonic level is\n"
"not magic: it carries the edge coloring in the operator itself, and what you would otherwise have to arrange by hand in the Pauli\n"
"terms (and keep arranged for every lattice) comes with the construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod padat mempunyai kedalaman rata dari $3\\times3$ ke atas (setiap warna ialah satu lapisan putaran $XX+YY$ bersebelahan; kekisi $2\\times2$\n"
"hanya mempunyai dua warna, jadi kedalamannya separuh) dan bilangan gate yang meningkat dengan bilangan ikatan.\n"
"Kod unari lebih mahal sebanyak satu magnitud dalam kedua-duanya. Sebabnya mudah: dalam kod padat, satu ikatan dipetakan kepada satu sebutan $XX$ dan\n"
"satu sebutan $YY$ pada dua qubit ikatan itu dengan pekali sama, iaitu putaran $XX+YY$ (dua `cz`). Dalam kod unari, setiap\n"
"mod mempunyai dua qubit (satu bagi setiap aras), dan lompatan berkembang menjadi beberapa rentetan Pauli berpemberat-4 pada empat qubit bagi kedua-dua\n"
"mod. Kesemuanya kalis tukar tertib, jadi tiada apa yang dijimatkan melalui kekalisan tukar tertib. Nisbah ini ialah sifat pengekodan pada $d = 2$, dan ia\n"
"tidak berubah dengan saiz kekisi. Pada $d = 2$, kod perduaan piawai dan kod Gray ialah kod yang sama, dan kod unari terunjur dan\n"
"tidak terunjur menghasilkan operator yang sama, jadi lengkung padat mewakili kedua-dua pasangan.\n"
"**Mengapa Trotterkan pada aras bosonik?** Lengkung putus-putus ialah langkah Trotter yang sama sebagai satu `PauliEvolutionGate` ke atas operator\n"
"qubit (bahagian 4), hijau untuk peringkat pertama dan biru untuk peringkat kedua. Lengkung biru pepejal ialah litar bosonik peringkat kedua,\n"
"lengkung hijau pepejal ialah yang peringkat pertama dari atas. Gate tunggal dengan sebutan disusun mengikut warna (pangkah) terletak tepat pada\n"
"lengkung bosonik peringkatnya: kedalaman rata (8 untuk peringkat pertama, 14 untuk peringkat kedua) dan bilangan gate minimum (seperti dalam bahagian sebelumnya). Qiskit tidak menemui\n"
"pengelompokan itu dengan sendirinya. Jika sebutan disenaraikan ikatan demi ikatan (segi empat sama), bilangan gate adalah sama, tetapi lapisan tidak dipadatkan\n"
"dan kedalaman meningkat dengan kekisi (pada $10\\times12$ ia ialah 84 berbanding 8 untuk peringkat pertama dan 166 berbanding 14 untuk peringkat kedua).\n"
"Dengan `preserve_order=False` (segi tiga), Qiskit memang menemui sebutan kalis tukar tertib dan kedalaman kekal rata, tetapi ia melayan sebutan XX dan YY\n"
"bagi satu ikatan sebagai putaran berasingan, jadi ia memerlukan kira-kira sepertiga lebih banyak gate dua-qubit dan dua kali ganda kedalaman. Jadi aras bosonik\n"
"bukan sihir: ia membawa pewarnaan tepi dalam operator itu sendiri, dan apa yang sebaliknya perlu anda susun secara manual dalam sebutan\n"
"Pauli (dan kekalkan susunannya bagi setiap kekisi) datang bersama pembinaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Transpile for Nighthawk {#6-transpile-for-nighthawk}"
msgstr "6. Transpile untuk Nighthawk {#6-transpile-for-nighthawk}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FakeNighthawk` is a $12\\times10$ square lattice with qubit index $10\\,\\text{row} + \\text{col}$. A hard-core lattice is a square\n"
"lattice too, so it sits on the chip as it is: site $(x, y)$ goes to qubit $10y + x$, which embeds an $L_x\\times L_y$ lattice\n"
"natively for $L_x \\le 10$, $L_y \\le 12$ as shown below.\n"
msgstr ""
"`FakeNighthawk` ialah kekisi segi empat sama $12\\times10$ dengan indeks qubit $10\\,\\text{row} + \\text{col}$. Kekisi teras keras ialah kekisi segi empat sama\n"
"juga, jadi ia terletak pada cip sebagaimana adanya: tapak $(x, y)$ pergi ke qubit $10y + x$, yang membenamkan kekisi $L_x\\times L_y$\n"
"secara natif untuk $L_x \\le 10$, $L_y \\le 12$ seperti ditunjukkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/3508477b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/hard-core-bosons-dynamics/extracted-outputs/3508477b-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, check the native embedding on the **unrouted** circuits. After lowering on the abstract register, every two-qubit gate must sit on a coupled pair under the layout.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, semak pembenaman natif pada litar **tanpa penghalaan**. Selepas penurunan pada daftar abstrak, setiap gate dua-qubit mesti terletak pada pasangan berganding di bawah susun atur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now route onto the chip. Every two-qubit gate is already on a coupler, so the transpiler has no swaps to insert and nothing to\n"
"choose: the routed circuit has the same two-qubit depth and the same two-qubit gate count as the circuit on the abstract\n"
"register, at every size. The cell below transpiles each lattice of the scaling study onto Nighthawk and asserts exactly that.\n"
"The drawing shows the routed circuit for the $4\\times4$ lattice. Each wire is labeled `q_i ↦ p`: virtual qubit `i` of the\n"
"encoded circuit (the lattice site `i`) sits on physical qubit `p` of the device at the start. Only the qubits the circuit acts\n"
"on are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang halakan ke atas cip. Setiap gate dua-qubit sudah berada pada pengganding, jadi transpiler tiada swap untuk disisipkan dan tiada apa untuk\n"
"dipilih: litar yang dihalakan mempunyai kedalaman dua-qubit dan bilangan gate dua-qubit yang sama seperti litar pada daftar\n"
"abstrak, pada setiap saiz. Sel di bawah mentranspile setiap kekisi kajian penskalaan ke atas Nighthawk dan menegaskan perkara itu dengan tepat.\n"
"Lukisan menunjukkan litar yang dihalakan untuk kekisi $4\\times4$. Setiap wayar dilabel `q_i ↦ p`: qubit maya `i` bagi\n"
"litar yang dikod (tapak kekisi `i`) terletak pada qubit fizikal `p` peranti pada permulaan. Hanya qubit yang digunakan litar\n"
"dilukis.\n"

