# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond hard-core bosons: higher mode truncation {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"
msgstr "7. Melangkaui boson teras keras: penggalan mod yang lebih tinggi {#7-beyond-hard-core-bosons-higher-mode-truncation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Everything so far only considered hard-core bosons, so the on-site term could not act. With $d = 3$, a site can\n"
"hold two bosons, $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ appears as a third group (diagonal), and the hopping matrix elements acquire $\\sqrt2$ factors.\n"
"The next cell builds the Bose-Hubbard step on a 4-site chain and measures its cost the same way, for all four encodings, next to the hard-core chain of the same length.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua yang setakat ini hanya mempertimbangkan boson teras keras, jadi sebutan dalam-tapak tidak dapat bertindak. Dengan $d = 3$, satu tapak boleh\n"
"memuatkan dua boson, $\\tfrac U2 n(n-1)$ muncul sebagai kumpulan ketiga (pepenjuru), dan unsur matriks lompatan\n"
"memperoleh faktor $\\sqrt2$.\n"
"Sel seterusnya membina langkah Bose-Hubbard pada rantai 4 tapak dan mengukur kosnya dengan cara yang sama, untuk keempat-empat pengekodan, di sebelah rantai teras keras dengan panjang yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The physics becomes significantly more complicated and the favorable scaling disappears.\n"
msgstr "Fizik menjadi jauh lebih rumit dan penskalaan yang menguntungkan itu lenyap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial used hard-core bosons because they make for simple analyses while emphasizing the benefits of the `qiskit-bosons` package and architecture of its transpiler framework. It is set up to investigate real bosonic physics beyond such simple truncation limits, but exploring these circuits and researching their application is now up to you.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan boson teras keras kerana ia memudahkan analisis sambil menekankan kelebihan pakej `qiskit-bosons` dan seni bina rangka kerja transpilernya. Ia disediakan untuk menyiasat fizik bosonik sebenar melangkaui had pemangkasan ringkas sedemikian, tetapi meneroka litar ini dan menyelidik aplikasinya kini terpulang kepada anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Takeaways and next steps {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"
msgstr "8. Rumusan dan langkah seterusnya {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output below recaps the circuit cost of a single Trotter step for the hard-core lattices, and the Trotter error of the small system.\n"
msgstr "Output di bawah merumuskan kos litar bagi satu langkah Trotter untuk kekisi teras keras, dan ralat Trotter bagi sistem kecil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From these numbers, you can draw some high-level takeaways. The first ones are about the framework, which is what you\n"
"carry over to other bosonic models. The later ones are about what the results show for hard-core bosons, the simple test case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada nombor ini, anda boleh membuat beberapa rumusan peringkat tinggi. Yang pertama berkaitan rangka kerja, iaitu apa yang\n"
"anda bawa ke model bosonik lain. Yang kemudian berkaitan apa yang ditunjukkan oleh keputusan untuk boson teras keras, kes ujian ringkas itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A framework for bosonic physics.** `qiskit-bosons` separates three things: the model (a `BosonOperator`, grouped here\n"
"by edge color), the circuit (one `Evolution` gate and a Trotter formula that splits it), and the lowering to qubits (the mode\n"
"truncation $d$ and the `LevelEncoding`, chosen when the transpiler preset runs). Changing one of them leaves the other two\n"
"untouched (sections 2 and 7).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Rangka kerja untuk fizik bosonik.** `qiskit-bosons` memisahkan tiga perkara: model (satu `BosonOperator`, dikelompokkan di sini\n"
"mengikut warna tepi), litar (satu gate `Evolution` dan formula Trotter yang memecahkannya), dan penurunan kepada qubit (penggalan\n"
"mod $d$ dan `LevelEncoding`, dipilih apabila praset transpiler dijalankan). Menukar satu daripadanya tidak menjejaskan dua yang lain\n"
"(bahagian 2 dan 7).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Why Trotterize at the bosonic level.** The grouping lives in the operator, so the Trotter circuit comes out with a flat depth\n"
"without any ordering by hand. One `PauliEvolutionGate` over the same qubit operator has the same Trotter error order and\n"
"scaling, and with the terms sorted by color it is the identical circuit. In another order, the depth grows with the lattice\n"
"(84 against 8 for one first-order step at $10\\times12$) or the gate count is about a third higher (sections 4 and 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mengapa Trotterkan pada aras bosonik.** Pengelompokan berada dalam operator, jadi litar Trotter terhasil dengan kedalaman rata\n"
"tanpa sebarang penyusunan manual. Satu `PauliEvolutionGate` ke atas operator qubit yang sama mempunyai peringkat ralat Trotter dan\n"
"penskalaan yang sama, dan dengan sebutan disusun mengikut warna ia ialah litar yang serupa. Dalam susunan lain, kedalaman meningkat dengan kekisi\n"
"(84 berbanding 8 untuk satu langkah peringkat pertama pada $10\\times12$) atau bilangan gate kira-kira sepertiga lebih tinggi (bahagian 4 dan 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Accuracy.** The only numerical error is the Trotter error between the colors, and it falls with the number of steps as\n"
"expected for first and second order (section 4). The qubit side and the encoding add nothing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ketepatan.** Satu-satunya ralat berangka ialah ralat Trotter antara warna, dan ia menurun dengan bilangan langkah seperti\n"
"dijangka untuk peringkat pertama dan kedua (bahagian 4). Bahagian qubit dan pengekodan tidak menambah apa-apa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The encoding is a cost choice.** At $d = 2$, all four encodings give the same physics. The compact codes need half the\n"
"qubits and are about 20 times cheaper in depth and gates than the unary ones (section 5).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengekodan ialah pilihan kos.** Pada $d = 2$, keempat-empat pengekodan memberikan fizik yang sama. Kod padat memerlukan separuh\n"
"qubit dan kira-kira 20 kali lebih murah dari segi kedalaman dan gate berbanding kod unari (bahagian 5).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hardware.** With the natural embedding of the lattice, every gate already sits on a Nighthawk coupler, so the chip runs the\n"
"circuit with no routing overhead at any size up to the whole chip (section 6).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Perkakasan.** Dengan pembenaman semula jadi kekisi, setiap gate sudah berada pada pengganding Nighthawk, jadi cip menjalankan\n"
"litar tanpa overhed penghalaan pada sebarang saiz sehingga keseluruhan cip (bahagian 6).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **Hard-core bosons are the entry point, not the goal.** They are the $U\\to\\infty$ limit of Bose-Hubbard, with the XY model as\n"
"  a spin-1/2 equivalent. They are exactly free fermions on an open chain but not on a square lattice, which makes 2D the\n"
"  interesting case (section 1). Raising the truncation to $d = 3$ brings the on-site interaction back and the cost jumps (a\n"
"  4-site chain goes from a two-qubit depth of 4 to 95 in the Gray code, section 7). That is where the exploration of bosonic\n"
"  physics begins, and the same framework carries it.\n"
"**Caveats.** All depths are for a noise-free fake backend (`FakeNighthawk`) and one fixed basis (`cz, rz, sx, x`, optimization\n"
"level 3); they compare structure, not fidelity. The routed numbers equal the abstract ones only because the natural embedding\n"
"puts every gate on a coupler. The Néel quench is one initial state; the Trotter error depends on the state and on $T$. Nothing\n"
"here runs on real hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"* **Boson teras keras ialah titik permulaan, bukan matlamat.** Ia ialah had $U\\to\\infty$ bagi Bose-Hubbard, dengan model XY sebagai\n"
"  setara spin-1/2. Ia ialah fermion bebas tepat pada rantai terbuka tetapi tidak pada kekisi segi empat sama, yang menjadikan 2D\n"
"  kes yang menarik (bahagian 1). Menaikkan penggalan kepada $d = 3$ membawa kembali interaksi dalam-tapak dan kos melonjak (satu\n"
"  rantai 4 tapak berubah daripada kedalaman dua-qubit 4 kepada 95 dalam kod Gray, bahagian 7). Di situlah penerokaan fizik\n"
"  bosonik bermula, dan rangka kerja yang sama membawanya.\n"
"**Perhatian.** Semua kedalaman adalah untuk backend palsu tanpa hingar (`FakeNighthawk`) dan satu asas tetap (`cz, rz, sx, x`, aras\n"
"pengoptimuman 3); ia membandingkan struktur, bukan kesetiaan. Nombor yang dihalakan sama dengan yang abstrak hanya kerana pembenaman semula jadi\n"
"meletakkan setiap gate pada pengganding. Kejutan Néel ialah satu keadaan awal; ralat Trotter bergantung pada keadaan dan pada $T$. Tiada apa pun di sini\n"
"yang dijalankan pada perkakasan sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next steps.** Hard-core bosons are a simple, checkable model to learn the framework on. From here, the same building\n"
"blocks apply to the models that are hard to treat classically:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah seterusnya.** Boson teras keras ialah model ringkas yang boleh disemak untuk mempelajari rangka kerja. Mulai sini, blok binaan\n"
"yang sama terpakai pada model yang sukar dirawat secara klasik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Larger cutoffs $d$ (soft-core bosons, the full Bose-Hubbard model), where the choice of encoding and of Trotter formula\n"
"matters much more than here (section 7)\n"
msgstr ""
"Penggalan $d$ yang lebih besar (boson teras lembut, model Bose-Hubbard penuh), di mana pilihan pengekodan dan formula Trotter\n"
"jauh lebih penting daripada di sini (bahagian 7)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Hamiltonians, such as bosons with a different interaction or a different coupling to their environment\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian lain, seperti boson dengan interaksi berbeza atau gandingan berbeza dengan persekitarannya\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other lattices, such as triangular or honeycomb, which need other edge colorings and other hardware embeddings\n"
msgstr "Kekisi lain, seperti segi tiga atau sarang lebah, yang memerlukan pewarnaan tepi dan pembenaman perkakasan yang lain\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Correlation functions as observables, such as $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ and density-density correlators\n"
msgstr "Fungsi korelasi sebagai observable, seperti $\\langle X_iX_j + Y_iY_j\\rangle$ dan korelator ketumpatan-ketumpatan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
